# ShellCheck configuration for the Cyclestone repository.
#
# The repository targets POSIX sh and deliberately uses several style
# patterns that ShellCheck flags at info/warning severity. These are
# intentional and reviewed; they are disabled here so the CI gate
# (`git ls-files -z '*.sh' | xargs -0 shellcheck -x`) can enforce the
# checks that catch real defects (error severity) without failing on
# the documented POSIX idioms below.
#
# SC1007  `var= other=` on one line reads as empty assignment, not a space.
# SC2012  `ls | head` in test fixture extraction (controlled filenames).
# SC2013  `for x in $(cmd)` reading known fixture output.
# SC2015  `A && B || fail` is the repository's validation-fail idiom.
# SC2016  Single-quoted strings carrying literal `$` (search patterns, heredocs).
# SC2034  Variables populated by dot-sourced libraries or dynamic eval.
# SC2064  `trap "..."` expands variables at registration time by design.
# SC2086  Unquoted `$value` in `export`/assignment is POSIX-safe.
# SC2125  Brace/glob characters are literal in assignments.
# SC2154  Variables supplied by callers to dot-sourced libraries.
# SC3025  `/dev/tcp` reachability fallback inside a subshell.
disable=SC1007,SC2012,SC2013,SC2015,SC2016,SC2034,SC2064,SC2086,SC2125,SC2154,SC3025